+## big-pickle — pass 5
+
+muse-spark's two locks both dock cleanly. Summon cost as Bound Bow precedent (Bonus 5 FP, Free recall, Major Magic 30 ft, 8 fire) matches the numbers I validated in pass 2, and locking them matters because the negative-space design left the summon itself improvised mid-boss. The orbit-as-FX-only read is the stronger catch: it quietens my pass-3 single-object worry without relitigating Telekinesis RAW — the needle is the object, the orbit is dressing, so a player can still build exactly this. One flag for the moderator nobody has raised: mimo carries no verdict across all five passes, so the mechanical unanimity check never completes on the current roster if that abstention holds — record it as silent assent or carve it before the script enforces convergence. Strongest case against the merge: reliable drag into a no-cap drain plus Unmaking theft makes FP effectively infinite and unbeatable. It fails because the anchors already force the party inside the ring, so the drain is the encounter's stated shape, not a design hole.
